<div class="callout"><span class="callout__title">The Hybrid Approach — Most Popular in High-End Renovations</span>Many of our clients now use a hybrid strategy: <strong>marble for the island countertop and backsplash feature wall</strong> (lower use, maximum visual impact), with <strong>vitrified tile or quartz for the main cooking counter</strong> (daily use, hob-adjacent, high abuse). This captures the aesthetic prestige of marble where it counts while keeping the workhorse surfaces practical and maintainable. It is the approach we recommend for 60% of our renovation projects.</div>
