<p>Section 06</p>
<h2>Pro Tips: What Interior Designers Do Differently</h2>
<p>After fifteen years and over 400 kitchen projects, here are the lessons that separate beautiful, functional kitchens from ones that photograph well but frustrate daily.</p>
<div class="callout callout--tip"><span class="callout__title">Tip</span><div class="callout callout--tip"><span class="callout__title">Tip</span>🗂️</p>
<h4>Zone Before You Buy</h4>
<p>Divide your kitchen into working zones: prep, cook, wash, serve, store. Every storage decision should serve one of these zones. Cross-zone storage creates friction and fatigue.</div>
<div class="callout callout--tip"><span class="callout__title">Tip</span>💧</p>
<h4>Moisture is the Enemy</h4>
<p>Always specify BWP (Boiling Water Proof) or marine ply for cabinet boxes. MDF swells. Cheap ply delaminates. In Indian kitchens, this is the single investment you cannot compromise.</div>
<div class="callout callout--tip"><span class="callout__title">Tip</span>🔦</p>
<h4>Light Inside Cabinets</h4>
<p>LED strip lighting inside deep wall cabinets and pull-out units is a tiny cost (₹500–₹2,000 per run) that transforms usability. You will use 20% more of your storage when you can see into it.</div>
<div class="callout callout--tip"><span class="callout__title">Tip</span>📐</p>
<h4>Measure Appliances First</h4>
<p>The number one cause of kitchen redesigns in year two: appliances that do not fit their designated space. Measure every appliance — pressure cooker, instant pot, rice cooker, mixer, oven — before your cabinet fabricator starts cutting boards.</div>
<div class="callout callout--tip"><span class="callout__title">Tip</span>🪣</p>
<h4>Bin Integration</h4>
<p>Built-in pull-out bins beneath the sink or beside the prep counter are significantly cleaner and more hygienic than freestanding waste bins. Plan for at least two compartments: wet waste and dry recyclables.</div>
<div class="callout callout--tip"><span class="callout__title">Tip</span>🎨</p>
<h4>The 70/30 Rule for Finishes</h4>
<p>70% of your surfaces should be in a calm, neutral finish. The remaining 30% is where you introduce personality — a bold backsplash, coloured lower cabinets, a statement island. This applies to marble vs tile decisions too.</div></div>
<div class="callout"><span class="callout__title">Most Overlooked Storage Area</span>The space between the top of your upper wall cabinets and the ceiling. In kitchens with 10-ft or higher ceilings, this dead zone can store everything from festival vessels to bulk dry goods in sealed containers. A simple enclosed loft unit costs ₹800–₹1,500 per running foot to fabricate and returns enormous value in a city apartment where every square foot matters.</div>
